Design a circuit that outputs an 8-bit signal based on the most significant bit (MSB) of the input. When the MSB (in[7]) is LOW, the output is set to 7F (0111 1111). When the MSB is HIGH, the output's MSB (out[7]) is inverted (producing a LOW), and the remaining bits (out[6:0]) are set to 0. This module primarily functions as a conditional output generator based on the input's MSB.
