description:
Develop a pipelined D flip-flop circuit that stages the input signal over three clock cycles before presenting it at the output. The design features three intermediate registers (d1, d2, d3) that capture the input data sequentially on each rising edge of the clock, effectively delaying the output by three clock cycles. The final output q reflects the value of the input d after being propagated through the pipeline, improving data processing time in synchronous systems.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output reg q
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input d,
    output reg q
);reg d1, d2, d3;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    d1 <= d;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    d2 <= d1;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    d3 <= d2;
end

always @(posedge clk) begin
    q <= d3;
end

endmodule

