description:
Design a voltage-controlled oscillator (VCO) that generates a square wave output frequency proportional to the input voltage (Vin). The center frequency of the oscillator is set at 1 MHz, with a sensitivity of 10 kHz/V. The VCO uses a clock input (clk) to increment a counter, and when the counter reaches a value determined by both Vin and the center frequency, it toggles the output signal (out). This functionality allows the oscillator's output frequency to vary linearly with the input voltage.
module top_module(
  input Vin,
  input clk,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input Vin,
  input clk,
  output out
);parameter f0 = 1000000; // center frequency of VCO
parameter k = 10000; // sensitivity of VCO

reg [31:0] counter;
reg out_reg;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  counter <= counter + 1;
  if (counter >= (f0 + k * Vin) / 2) begin
    out_reg <= ~out_reg;
    counter <= 0;
  end
end

assign out = out_reg;

endmodule

