Design a 4-bit binary to 7-segment display decoder. The module takes a 4-bit input representing a hexadecimal digit (0 to F) and outputs the corresponding 8-bit control signal for illuminating the segments of a 7-segment display. Each output configuration for the segments is defined in a case structure, ensuring that the appropriate segments are activated for each input value, with a default condition to turn off all segments for invalid inputs.
