description:
Design a circuit that counts the number of consecutive high (1) bits in a 4-bit input. The module outputs a 3-bit value representing the count of consecutive 1s from the most significant bit. The counting resets when a 0 is encountered, and the output will reflect a maximum count of 3, corresponding to the sequences of 1s detected. The circuit incorporates a state to track the previous input condition to determine if the counting should continue or reset.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output [2:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output [2:0] out
);reg [2:0] count;
reg prev;

always @(in) begin
    if (in == 4'b0000) begin
        count <= 3'b000;
        prev <= 1'b0;
    end
    else if (in == 4'b1111) begin
        count <= 3'b111;
        prev <= 1'b1;
    end
    else if (in[3] & in[2] & in[1] & in[0]) begin
        count <= 3'b100;
        prev <= 1'b1;
    end
    else if (in[3] & in[2] & in[1] & ~in[0] & prev) begin
        count <= 3'b011;
        prev <= 1'b1;
    end
    else if (in[3] & in[2] & ~in[1] & prev) begin
        count <= 3'b010;
        prev <= 1'b1;
    end
    else if (in[3] & ~in[2] & prev) begin
        count <= 3'b001;
        prev <= 1'b1;
    end
    else begin
        count <= 3'b000;
        prev <= 1'b0;
    end
end

assign out = count;

endmodule

